omphalomesenteric.d:
a. Of or pertaining to the umbilicus and mesentery;
   omphalomesaraic; as, the omphalomesenteric arteries and veins of a
   fetus.

osmic.d:
a. Pertaining to, derived from, or containing, osmium;
   specifically, designating those compounds in which it has a valence
   higher than in other lower compounds; as, osmic oxide.

overfullness.d:
n. The state of being excessively or abnormally full, so
   as to cause overflow, distention, or congestion; excess of fullness;
   surfeit.
